Subject: [PATCH] Pin the shared-media panel's own continuation rule

The shared-media redesign suppresses continuations for the File timeline in
every layout, and says so where it does it: a filtered file list is not a
conversation, so each row keeps its own avatar and sender. The upstream case
still asserted that bubble layout lets continuations through, which is the
behaviour the early return exists to prevent.

The assertion never failed before because the file it lives in sat at a path
no runner collected. Co-locating the tests is what surfaced it, so this is an
old contradiction being read for the first time rather than a new regression.

Recorded here so the integration branch is honest about what the fork does.
The branch that introduced the behaviour still carries the upstream assertion
and will fail CI there until it takes the same change.
